From e7fcee5da6f0ec4cb31ef01969eedf3c678712d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Starbite build <build@starbite.invalid>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:31:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] 0171: the on-disk shader cache on Windows (GL kit):
 -Dshader-cache=enabled builds there

Mesa refuses the shader cache on Windows (meson) and has no file code for it
(disk_cache_os.c: "TODO"); Panfrost names a driver build by its ELF build-id
note, which a PE image does not have.

- util: disk_cache_os_portable.c, the multi-file cache on a dozen file
  primitives (Win32 on UTF-8 paths; POSIX only for the unit tests, with
  -DSB_DISK_CACHE_PORTABLE_TEST). Same directory layout and entry bytes as on
  Linux. An entry that does not check out is deleted and written again; the
  size counter is counted again once per process on the cache thread; the
  time of last use is written by us; default directory
  %LOCALAPPDATA%\Starbite\shader-cache\mesa_shader_cache.
- util: no zlib/zstd needed: entries are stored as they are (CRC and length
  checked on every read).
- util: disk_cache_pe_image_identifier / disk_cache_get_module_identifier:
  the identity of a driver build from the PE headers (link time stamp, sizes,
  section table), the same for the file, the loaded image, and both views of
  an ARM64X image.
- panfrost: that identity + Mesa version + git commit is the driver id on
  Windows; a cache that is off is dropped (state tracker path as before);
  log lines: on/off with directory, limit and id; counters every 32 lookups,
  at the first frame and at process end.
- wgl: C:\ProgramData\Starbite\glnocache or SB_GL_SHADER_CACHE=0 turns it off.
- tests: cache_test.cpp: damaged entries, driver id change, unusable
  directory, recount at start, the limit, the PE identity.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
